\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}$\mathbb N=\{1,2,\ldots\}$, and $\mathbb Z,\mathbb Q,\mathbb R,\mathbb C$ denote the integers, rationals, reals and complex numbers. Any other conventions are specified locally.


Write $\mathbb D=\{z\in\mathbb C:|z|<1\}$ and $\mathbb T=\partial\mathbb D$. Let $S_H$ consist of injective, sense-preserving harmonic functions on $\mathbb D$ with the expansion
\[f(z)=\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}a_nz^n+\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}a_{-n}\overline z^{\,n},\qquad a_1=1.\]
Harmonicity means that the real and imaginary parts satisfy the planar Laplace equation. Writing $f=h+\overline g$ with $h,g$ holomorphic, sense preservation is $|h'(z)|^2-|g'(z)|^2>0$ throughout $\mathbb D$. The subclass $S_H^0$ is defined by $a_{-1}=0$.

\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For every $f\in S_H^0$ and integer $n\geq2$, does
\[\bigl||a_n|-|a_{-n}|\bigr|\leq n\]
hold? The outer absolute value is part of the assertion. \href{https://arxiv.org/abs/1809.07200}{[S2]} \href{https://arxiv.org/abs/1403.5619}{[S3]}

\subsection{Short English statement}
Is the absolute difference between the magnitudes of the analytic and coanalytic nth coefficients at most n?

\subsection{Sources}
